From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mangoapp: keep a lease client off the shared queue

Every gamescope opens the mangoapp queue with ftok("mangoapp", 65), a
relative path that normally does not exist, so all of them share key -1.
A --drm-lease-client gamescope driving a companion panel then fed its
frame stats and focused pid into the main session's mangoapp, which
reported the wrong app and, for a non-dumpable one, aborted reading its
fdinfo.

A lease client never runs a mangoapp, so it no longer opens the queue.
The id starts at -1 instead of 0, a valid queue id, so every send and
receive in that instance fails harmlessly.
---
diff --git a/src/mangoapp.cpp b/src/mangoapp.cpp
index e7c7ede5..32a67ee1 100644
--- a/src/mangoapp.cpp
+++ b/src/mangoapp.cpp
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 #include "main.hpp"
 
 static bool inited = false;
-static int msgid = 0;
+static int msgid = -1;
 static std::mutex s_SnapshotMutex;
 static std::unordered_map<uint32_t, MangoappSnapshot_t> s_ConnectorSnapshots;
 extern bool g_bAppWantsHDRCached;
@@ -48,8 +48,11 @@ struct mangoapp_msg_v1 {
 } __attribute__((packed));
 
 void init_mangoapp(){
-    int key = ftok("mangoapp", 65);
-    msgid = msgget(key, 0666 | IPC_CREAT);
+    // A lease client must not feed the session's shared mangoapp queue
+    if (!g_sDrmLeaseClientSocket) {
+        int key = ftok("mangoapp", 65);
+        msgid = msgget(key, 0666 | IPC_CREAT);
+    }
     inited = true;
 }
 
